；輕柔的"],[45,"sniff","snɪf","v.","嗅；聞"],[46,"groom","grum","v.","理毛；梳理"],[47,"escalate","ˈɛskəˌlet","v.","升級；加劇"],[48,"urgent","ˈɝdʒənt","a.","緊急的；急迫的"],[49,"targeted","ˈtɑrgɪtɪd","a.","有針對性的"],[50,"intervention","ˌɪntɚˈvɛnʃən","n.","介入；處置"],[51,"bite","baɪt","v.","咬；叮"],[52,"actively","ˈæktɪvlɪ","ad.","積極地；主動地"],[53,"pull","pʊl","v.","拉；拔"],[54,"companion","kəmˈpænjən","n.","同伴；伴侶"],[55,"tongue","tʌŋ","n.","舌頭；語言"],[56,"instinctive","ɪnˈstɪŋktɪv","a.","本能的；直覺的"],[57,"maneuver","məˈnuvɚ","n.","動作；手法"],[58,"prevent","prɪˈvɛnt","v.","預防；阻止"],[59,"choke","tʃok","v.","窒息；噎住"],[60,"significantly","sɪgˈnɪfəkəntlɪ","ad.","顯著地；重大地"],[61,"accelerate","ækˈsɛləˌret","v.","加速；促進"],[62,"recovery","rɪˈkʌvərɪ","n.","復原；恢復"],[63,"unconscious","ʌnˈkɑnʃəs","a.","失去知覺的"],[64,"notably","ˈnotəblɪ","ad.","顯著地；特別是"],[65,"aggressive","əˈgrɛsɪv","a.","侵略性的"],[66,"once","wʌns","conj.","一旦；一經"],[67,"fall","fɔl","v.","倒下；落下"],[68,"regain","rɪˈgen","v.","重新獲得；恢復"],[69,"normal","ˈnɔrmḷ","a.","正常的；常規的"],[70,"interaction","ˌɪntɚˈækʃən","n.","互動；相互作用"],[71,"resume","rɪˈzjum","v.","恢復；重新開始"],[72,"injury","ˈɪndʒərɪ","n.","傷害；損害"],[73,"hrough","θru","prep.","透過；經由"],[74,"advanced","ədˈvænst","a.","先進的；高等的"],[75,"neural","ˈnjʊrəl","a.","神經系統的"],[76,"imaging","ˈɪmɪdʒɪŋ","n.","造影；成像"],[77,"optogenetics","ˌɑptodʒəˈnɛtɪks","n.","光遺傳學"],[78,"researcher","riˈsɝtʃɚ","n.","研究員；調查者"],[79,"prosocial","proˈsoʃəl","a.","造福社會的"],[80,"be driven by","bi ˈdrɪvn baɪ","ph.","受...驅使"],[81,"oxytocin","ˌɑksɪˈtosɪn","n.","催產素"],[82,"commonly","ˈkɑmənlɪ","ad.","通常；普遍地"],[83,"refer to as","rɪˈfɝ tu æz","ph.","稱作；稱為"],[84,"hormone","ˈhɔrmon","n.","荷爾蒙；激素"],[85,"associated with","əˈsoʃɪˌetɪd wɪð","ph.","與...有關聯的"],[86,"bonding","ˈbɑndɪŋ","n.","緊密關係建立"],[87,"empathy","ˈɛmpəθɪ","n.","同理心；共鳴"],[88,"significantly","sɪgˈnɪfəkəntlɪ","ad.","顯著地；極大地"],[89,"pronounced","prəˈnaʊnst","a.","明顯的；顯著的"],[90,"familiar","fəˈmɪljɚ","a.","熟悉的；親密的"],[91,"cage-mate","kedʒ met","n.","同籠夥伴；籠友"],[92,"social","ˈsoʃəl","a.","社會的；群居的"],[93,"attachment","əˈtætʃmənt","n.","依附；依戀"],[94,"play a key role in","ple ə ki rol ɪn","ph.","在...中扮演關鍵角色"],[95,"the drive to","ðə draɪv tu","ph.","去做...的動力"],[96,"rescue","ˈrɛskju","v.","營救；援救"],[97,"cognition","kɑgˈnɪʃən","n.","認知；認識"],[98,"rudimentary","ˌrudəˈmɛntərɪ","a.","基本的；初級的"],[99,"instinct","ˈɪnstɪŋkt","n.","本能；直覺"],[100,"empathetic","ˌɛmpəˈθɛtɪk","a.","具同理心的"],[101,"evolve","ɪˈvɑlv","v.","演化；逐步發展"],[102,"vertebrate","ˈvɝtəbrɪt","n.","脊椎動物"],[103,"previously","ˈprivɪəslɪ","ad.","先前地；以前"]],"S":[{"a":0,"h":"第 1 段","p":[["@Can Mice [Perform CPR|1]? Scientists [Discover|2] [Rodents|3] Providing First Aid","小鼠會進行心肺復甦術嗎？科學家發現囓齒動物也能提供急救"],["When humans [encounter|4] an [unconscious|5] person, their [immediate|6] [instinct|7] is often to check for breathing, [call for|8] medical [assistance|9], or [initiate|10] [cardiopulmonary|11] [resuscitation|12] (CPR).","當人類遇到昏迷者時，他們的第一個反應通常是檢查呼吸、呼叫醫療救助或進行心肺復甦術（CPR）。"],["[For decades|13], [complex|14] [emergency|15] [interventions|16] like clearing an [obstructed|17] [airway|18] were believed to be [unique|19] to humans and a few higher [primates|20].","幾十年來，人們一直認為像清除阻塞氣道這樣複雜的緊急幹預措施是人類和少數高等靈長類動物所獨有的。"],["However, a [landmark|21] study [published|22] in the [journal|23] Science has [revealed|24] that mice are also [capable of|25] performing [life-saving|26] [first aid|27] on their [peers|28].","然而，發表在《科學》雜誌上的一項里程碑式研究表明，小鼠也能夠對同伴進行救命的急救。"],["The [discovery|29] [occurred|30] almost by accident at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California (USC).","這項發現幾乎是偶然發生的，地點在南加州大學凱克醫學院。"],["While [observing|31] [paired|32] rodents during [laboratory|33] experiments, [neuroscientists|34] noticed an [extraordinary|35] pattern of behavior when one mouse [lost consciousness|36].","在實驗室實驗中觀察成對的囓齒動物時，神經科學家注意到，當其中一隻小鼠失去意識時，它表現出一種非同尋常的行為模式。"]]},{"a":1,"h":"第 2 段","p":[["[Rather than|37] [abandoning|38] the [unresponsive|39] peer, the conscious \"helper mouse\" [immediately|40] [initiated|41] [a sequence of|42] rescue actions.","清醒的「救助鼠」並沒有拋棄失去意識的同伴，而是立即採取了一系列救援行動。"],["The [response|43] began with [gentle|44] [sniffing|45] and [grooming|46], quickly [escalating|47] to more [urgent|48] and [targeted|49] [interventions|50].","救援行動最初以輕柔的嗅聞和梳理開始，隨後迅速升級為更緊急、更有針對性的干預措施。"],["Helper mice were observed [biting|51] near the mouth and [actively|52] [pulling|53] the unconscious [companion|54]'s [tongue|55] forward.","觀察發現，救援小鼠會咬住昏迷同伴的嘴部附近，並主動將同伴的舌頭拉向前。"],["By clearing the airway, this [instinctive|56] [maneuver|57] helped [prevent|58] [choking|59] and [significantly|60] [accelerated|61] the [recovery|62] time of the [unconscious|63] mouse.","這種本能行為透過清理呼吸道，幫助防止窒息，並顯著加快了昏迷小鼠的恢復速度。"],["[Notably|64], this behavior was not [aggressive|65]; [once|66] the [fallen|67] mouse [regained|68] consciousness, [normal|69] [interaction|70] [resumed|71] without [injury|72].","值得注意的是，這種行為並不具有攻擊性；一旦跌倒的小鼠恢復意識，正常的互動便會恢復，且未造成任何傷害。"]]},{"a":2,"h":"第 3 段","p":[["[Through|73] [advanced|74] [neural|75] [imaging|76] and [optogenetics|77], the [researchers|78] discovered that this [prosocial|79] behavior [is driven by|80] [oxytocin|81] — [commonly|82] [referred to as|83] the \"love [hormone|84]\" [associated with|85] social [bonding|86] and [empathy|87].","研究人員利用先進的神經影像和光遺傳學技術發現，這種親社會行為是由催產素驅動的——催產素通常被稱為 “愛情荷爾蒙”，與社會連結和同理心密切相關。"],["The emergency response was [significantly|88] more [pronounced|89] between [familiar|90] [cage-mates|91], proving that [social|92] [attachment|93] [plays a key role in|94] [the drive to|95] [rescue|96] others.","這種緊急救援反應在熟悉的籠伴之間更為顯著，證明社會依戀在救助他人的驅動力中扮演關鍵角色。"],["This study challenges traditional views of animal [cognition|97], suggesting that [rudimentary|98] first-aid [instincts|99] and [empathetic|100] behaviors may have [evolved|101] far earlier in [vertebrate|102] history than [previously|103] understood.","這項研究挑戰了關於動物認知能力的傳統觀點，顯示基本的急救本能和同理心行為可能在脊椎動物演化史上出現的時間比之前認為的要早得多。"]]}],"K":[[[[0.21,0],[0.63,0.06],[1.1,0.12],[1.78,0.224],[3.46,0.373],[4.19,0.478],[4.83,0.627],[5.53,0.731],[6.26,0.88],[6.58,0.94],[6.98,1]],[[8.2